Produce a NEW production sprite atlas from the supplied ONE character reference. EXACTLY TEN separate full-body poses of the SAME character, arranged in a precise regular grid of FIVE columns and TWO rows, read left-to-right then top-to-bottom. Wide transparent canvas approximately 2560 by 1024, 5:2 aspect ratio. No labels, numbers, panel outlines, background, vignette, cast shadow, glow, horizon, floor marks or checkerboard baked into pixels. Real transparent background with clean cutout alpha around each whole sprite. Ten isolated sprites only, ONE sprite in each equally sized cell with generous transparent padding on every side, at least 8% empty gutter. Do NOT let tails, claws or head cross a cell boundary. Keep the exact recognizable anatomy, proportions, palette and tightly shaded detailed retro sprite rendering of the provided reference, no redesign or photoreal restyle. All sprites are strict side-view or the same slight side angle as the source, ALL FACING RIGHT, head pointing right and tail behind to the left. Use ONE CONSTANT PIXEL SCALE for the organism in every cell: the head/skull length must stay equal across standing, walking, attacking and lying poses. Never enlarge a short KO pose to fill a cell. Feet or the lowest supported body point align to the SAME horizontal ground height near 90% of cell height in every cell; nothing extends beneath that support plane. Keep the entire long tail inside each frame by bending it naturally, not chopping it or shortening it. Preserve coherent bright edges and the original metallic detailed shading. The grid positions are:
TOP ROW, columns 1–5:
1 idle neutral alert stance;
2 walk contact A, near leg or limb extended forward;
3 walk contact B, opposite leg or limb forward, visibly distinct limb positions from cell 2;
4 primary CLAW strike windup, forelimb pulled back and body braced;
5 primary CLAW strike impact, ONE forelimb extended forward to the right with fingers open, natural reach, rest of body remains same size.
BOTTOM ROW, columns 1–5:
6 claw strike recovery, forelimb returning and weight settling; distinct from idle;
7 guard braced, forelimbs held defensively in front of torso/head;
8 hit recoil, spine bends back and forelimbs lifted slightly, still recognizable and supported;
9 KO falling phase: knees/elbows buckling, head and chest descending towards the ground; low collapsed pose, not a standing character tilted;
10 KO final: entire creature genuinely lying horizontally on its SIDE, torso, shoulder and long skull low on the same ground plane, limbs folded and tail resting low; unmistakably fully prone, not crouching or kneeling. No gore, severing or damage effects.
The attack is the ordinary physical claw strike ONLY, never an acid special, tail special or a super animation. Ten coherent new drawings with real changed joint poses. Do not repeat the same standing silhouette across the action cells.

